====Noun====
{{wp|Toque (French)|toque}}
{{en-noun}}

# A type of [[hat]] with no [[brim]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1824|title=La Belle Assemblée|volume=29|month=January|section=Fashions|page=32|text='''Toques''' are for the most part indented in the mural style, in two rows, between which are placed marabout feathers. Flowers, feathers, ears of corn, in gold or silver: such are the chief ornaments on the heads of young ladies, either as separate decorations or all blended together. Black velvet '''toques''' are ornamented with marabout feathers of a light grey, mingled with a few ears of gold corn.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1903|author=Janet Elder Rait|title=Alison Howard|publisher=Archibald Constable & Co.|page=273
|passage="Because Esmé said she was going out this afternoon to choose a new '''toque''', and she hoped I should like it, and I’m not quite sure what it is, or where she'll wear it. Do you mind explaining?"<br>"Not at all. A '''toque''' is that which if it had strings would be a bonnet, and if it had brim, would be a hat. It is worn on the head."<br>"Thanks, now I know where I am," said the vicar of St. Machars, with a sigh of relief.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1932|translator=Vyvyan Holland|title=The Strange River|author=Julien Green|publisher=Harper & Brothers|page=180
|passage=She drank a glass of wine mixed with water, took off her felt '''toque''' and her shoes, and slid beneath the red eiderdown.}}
#* '''1957'''—[[w:Samuel Beckett|Samuel Beckett]], [[w:Endgame (play)|"Endgame"]],
#*: In a dressing-gown, a stiff '''toque''' on his head, a large blood-stained handkerchief over his face, a whistle hanging from his neck, a rug over his knees, thick socks on his feet, Hamm seems to be asleep.
# {{lb|en|specifically}} A [[tall]] [[white]] [[hat]] with no [[brim]] of the sort [[wear|worn]] by [[chef]]s
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Michael Ruhlman|title=The Making of a Chef: Mastering Heat at the Culinary Institute of America|publisher=Owl Books|isbn=0805061738|page=154
|passage=Chef Felder was in her early forties, slender, with short wavy brown hair, almost all of which could be contained within her '''toque'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Jerrilyn Farmer|title=Killer Wedding|publisher=HarperCollins|isbn=0380795981|page=103
|passage=When I came to the back of a man's head, wearing a '''toque''', I knew I'd spotted my quarry.<br>"Chef Reynoso?"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Laura Levine|title=Killer Blonde|publisher=Kensington Books|isbn=0758201621|page=114
|passage=Minutes later, a red-faced man in a chef's '''toque''' approached our table.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|informal}} A [[chef]].
#* '''2007'''—October, Nicole Berrie, "Green Eggs and Sam", in [[w:Elle|''Elle'']], page 360,
#*: Sam Mason first grabbed the spotlight as the pastry chef ... for being the most rock 'n' roll '''toque''' in town.
# A variety of [[bonnet monkey]]; {{vern|toque macaque}}, {{taxlink|Macaca sinica|species}}.
# {{lb|en|historical}} An African nominal money of account, equal to 40 [[cowry|cowries]].

