===Etymology 2===
1871. Assimilated from {{bor|en|fr-CA|tuque}}. Likely to be a {{glossary|hypercorrection}} from the time that {{m|en|toque}} was already in the dictionaries when they did not yet list {{m|en|tuque}} as a kind of hat. The French word {{m|fr|tuque}} for hat is itself not strictly a deformation of French {{m|fr|toque}}: it is also related to other meanings of ''tuque'' and to its former name ''bonnet à la turque'' (lit. Turkish-style bunnet/cap).

